diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8db45e3224..7278f4a7a2 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -423,6 +423,13 @@ Setup also installs [audio.cpp](https://github.com/0xShug0/audio.cpp) (prebuilt
 - `UNSLOTH_AUDIO_CPP_ACCELERATOR=cpu` (or `cuda`, `vulkan`, `metal`) picks the bundle instead of auto-detecting.
 - `AUDIOCPP_SERVER_PATH=/path/to/audiocpp_server` uses your own build.
 
+#### AMD Ryzen AI NPU:
+
+On a Ryzen AI PC with an XDNA2 NPU (Linux x86_64 or Windows, NPU driver installed), Studio runs chat models on the NPU through [FastFlowLM](https://github.com/ROCm/FastFlowLM) and [Lemonade](https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/lemonade), separately from the GPU:
+- In Chat, open **Select model**: the **NPU** group has an **Enable NPU** button that downloads Lemonade and FastFlowLM (about 47 MB) and checks the driver. Clicking an NPU model then downloads and loads it. The Model hub lists them under **Browse NPU models**.
+- From a terminal: `unsloth run --model qwen3-0.6b-FLM`, or `unsloth chat qwen3-0.6b-FLM` while Studio is running.
+- Over the API, NPU models serve `/v1/chat/completions` as `lemonade:<id>` (for example `lemonade:qwen3-0.6b-FLM`). With **Switch model by request** on (Settings > API), naming a downloaded NPU model loads it. They do not take `response_format`, `seed`, `frequency_penalty` or `logprobs`, and the coding agents in `unsloth start` need a GGUF model.
+
 #### Uninstall
 
 **MacOS, WSL, Linux:** `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unslothai/unsloth/main/scripts/uninstall.sh | sh`
